# Reviewed example only. NOT INSTALLED BY ANYTHING, and not by G4.
#
# Installing a sudoers drop-in is gate G3. This file exists so the grant can be
# reviewed as text before it is policy, and so that "what exactly did we agree
# to give away?" has a written answer.
#
# The accepted authority is exactly one sentence:
#
#   cschott may execute exactly the Kyri transition helper with exactly one
#   valid CINV identity.
#
# It is not general passwordless root, not switch-user authority, and not a
# grant over any other Kyri helper. kyri-exec-quota and kyri-exec-admin are
# deliberately absent: the quota operation runs inside the transition that this
# rule already authorises, and the administrative helper is interactively
# authenticated with no NOPASSWD at all.
#
# Boundary specification §3.2 and §3.3 are normative for every property below.
#
# --- required properties, and why -------------------------------------------
#
# exact absolute path        never a directory, never ALL, never a wildcard
# one caller, one runas      cschott, and root only
# regex argument             ^CINV-[0-9]{6}$ -- sudoers 1.9 treats an argument
#                            beginning with ^ as a regular expression, so the
#                            policy layer refuses a malformed identity before
#                            the helper is executed at all
# NOPASSWD                   the coordinator is non-interactive; ruling R4
#                            accepts it for this one reviewed helper only
# env_reset in force         no env_keep addition, no SETENV; the helper trusts
#                            none of the surviving variables and constructs the
#                            worker environment explicitly
# no shell, no !authenticate beyond NOPASSWD
#
# Argument validation is NOT delegated to this file. The helper independently
# revalidates ^CINV-[0-9]{6}$; the regex here is defence in depth, because a
# policy layer that is the only validator is one syntax error away from being
# no validator.
#
# --- integrity ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Primary control is immutable root-owned ancestry: the helper and every
# writable ancestor are root:root and non-writable by cschott, by
# kyri-capability, and by any unprivileged user or group. sudoers(5) is explicit
# that a grant over a command the user can write is void -- a digest cannot
# repair a writable binary.
#
# Secondary control is the SHA-256 digest below, defence in depth and never a
# substitute for that ancestry. sudo's fdexec default is digest_only, so the
# descriptor that was hashed is the one executed and the hash-then-swap race is
# closed by the mechanism rather than by our code.
#
# The digest is captured at G3 from the INSTALLED artifact and pasted here. It
# is deliberately a placeholder in the repository: a real-looking digest
# committed as an example is one somebody ships by accident. A helper upgrade
# that changes it is an intentional review event, and the transition fails
# closed on mismatch.
#
# Capture it with:
#     sha256sum /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-transition
#
# Install (G3 only) as /etc/sudoers.d/kyri-exec, root:root, mode 0440, and
# validate with `visudo -c -f` BEFORE moving it into place.

Cmnd_Alias KYRI_EXEC_TRANSITION = sha256:REPLACE_WITH_INSTALLED_HELPER_DIGEST /usr/libexec/kyri-exec-transition ^CINV-[0-9]{6}$

cschott ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: KYRI_EXEC_TRANSITION
